WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.320
Peace be upon you and welcome to all of you. This is the final video in which we conclude the first phase of our fellowship.

00:07.760 --> 00:15.080
Our journey in the previous sections focused on understanding the health educator's role and analyzing community needs, reaching effective communication.

00:15.080 --> 00:22.260
Yet today we are placing the foundation stone that protects all these skills: ethical grounding and professional responsibility.

00:22.760 --> 00:27.080
Health and climate education is not merely two words we write in a post on social media and that is all.

00:27.080 --> 00:34.280
This is a genuine commitment and people's lives. Let us see how ethics is the backbone of any genuinely impactful communication.

00:35.000 --> 00:39.860
Imagine with me this situation: Just one erroneous piece of information about a magical home cure is posted online.

00:40.160 --> 00:42.960
And in seconds, it spreads like wildfire.

00:43.320 --> 00:47.220
This simple error on the screen transforms into very real harm on the ground.

00:47.580 --> 00:54.180
And a word emerging from any awareness platform can cause entire families to make wrong decisions that harm their future and health.

00:54.180 --> 00:57.060
That is why the responsibility of the word here is immense.

00:57.420 --> 01:02.380
And we must be one million percent sure of the accuracy and credibility of any information we publish.

01:02.500 --> 01:06.460
In this explanation, we will walk along a fast and important map.

01:06.780 --> 01:08.460
Let us enter the first topic immediately:

01:08.900 --> 01:11.400
The power of information and the impact of the word in awareness.

01:11.800 --> 01:14.820
To understand this power, the equation is simple yet critical:

01:15.220 --> 01:18.140
Ethics equals trust plus responsibility.

01:18.540 --> 01:20.620
Trust is our true balance.

01:20.620 --> 01:24.100
When people follow us, they automatically assume that we are

01:24.180 --> 01:25.280
a safe and reliable source.

01:25.560 --> 01:27.940
So ethics is not some theorizing and idealism;

01:28.260 --> 01:31.920
it is the solid shield that protects people from myths and personal conjecture.

01:32.320 --> 01:36.060
It fights misinformation and helps the community make sound and healthy decisions.

01:36.460 --> 01:39.420
And this is precisely what builds our credibility to last for years.

01:40.040 --> 01:43.800
And this brings us to a very sensitive point, which is in the second section:

01:44.160 --> 01:46.560
The health educator versus the clinical doctor,

01:46.780 --> 01:48.140
and the boundaries of our professional role.

01:48.140 --> 01:50.600
We must be completely clear on this point,

01:50.600 --> 01:53.160
in order to maintain the safety of the health system and the people.

01:53.560 --> 01:57.920
The health educator is not a replacement for a doctor, a nurse, or a clinical therapist.

01:58.340 --> 02:00.160
Our great role is centered on awareness,

02:00.480 --> 02:01.680
simplifying difficult sciences,

02:02.120 --> 02:03.720
building a bridge for understanding,

02:04.100 --> 02:06.480
and directing people to the right sources and clinics.

02:06.760 --> 02:11.900
As for individual diagnosis, writing prescriptions for medications, or intervening in a medical treatment plan:

02:12.240 --> 02:13.120
This is a red line,

02:13.440 --> 02:15.600
and the exclusive domain of physicians and specialists.

02:15.860 --> 02:17.700
True professionalism

02:17.700 --> 02:21.620
begins with knowing the boundaries of our role well and never exceeding them under any circumstance.

02:22.420 --> 02:24.280
Well, since we know our role now,

02:24.400 --> 02:26.900
how do we verify the words we speak?

02:26.900 --> 02:28.700
In the third section: Verifying sources,

02:29.500 --> 02:31.160
your guide to reliable information.

02:31.580 --> 02:33.380
Before we click the publish button for any piece of information,

02:33.680 --> 02:36.660
we must pass it through a filter of four essential questions:

02:37.020 --> 02:37.700
Where did this information come from?

02:38.500 --> 02:40.940
Is it issued by an official scientific entity?

02:40.940 --> 02:42.700
Is it recent and aligned with new developments?

02:42.700 --> 02:46.560
And is it built on robust evidence and studies?

02:46.560 --> 02:48.960
Our references are always the major scientific bodies,

02:49.320 --> 02:53.700
such as the World Health Organization, United Nations climate and environmental bodies,

02:54.420 --> 02:56.560
and peer-reviewed medical journals and universities.

02:56.860 --> 03:01.080
Conversely, anonymous WhatsApp messages and random social media posts:

03:01.080 --> 03:03.880
relying on them destroys credibility in a second,

03:04.240 --> 03:06.080
and they have no place in our work.

03:06.080 --> 03:10.080
Well, what if we find erroneous information spreading, how do we act?

03:10.080 --> 03:11.160
In the fourth section:

03:11.160 --> 03:15.820
We live in an age of digital chaos, and rumors travel faster than the truth.

03:16.180 --> 03:20.320
We hear claims like: "Climate change is a hoax and media gossip,"

03:20.320 --> 03:22.640
or "Heat has no relationship to heart attacks."

03:23.060 --> 03:28.620
The golden rule says: Focus on facts, evidence, and empathy, and stay away from polemics.

03:28.960 --> 03:33.620
The goal is not to enter a stubborn fight to prove who is right and who is wrong, nor to ridicule anyone.

03:33.980 --> 03:38.560
The goal is to build bridges of understanding and deliver the correct information with gentle, respectful manners

03:38.560 --> 03:41.520
that make the other party open their mind and heart when they hear us.

03:41.520 --> 03:46.560
We listen to their concerns with empathy, and present the truth clearly and with solid evidence.

03:46.940 --> 03:50.680
And this takes us to the fifth section: Empowering climate communication.

03:51.020 --> 03:55.520
Empowerment, not intimidation: When talking about climate, it is very easy to fall into the trap of fear-mongering,

03:56.180 --> 03:59.500
and speak about the end of the world and disasters to grab attention.

03:59.880 --> 04:02.440
Yet in all honesty, this method yields the opposite result:

04:02.440 --> 04:06.680
It paralyzes people, makes them feel helpless and despairing, and leads them to ignore the issue.

04:07.060 --> 04:09.040
The solution is empowering communication:

04:09.400 --> 04:11.560
We acknowledge the challenge and state reality,

04:11.880 --> 04:15.300
yet we focus more on preventive steps and feasible solutions.

04:15.620 --> 04:21.240
Instead of saying: "The future is a catastrophe with no hope," we say responsibly: "Climate change is a real challenge,

04:21.520 --> 04:24.600
yet with simple steps, we can protect our families and mitigate the danger."

04:24.960 --> 04:28.460
Our goal is to build hope and the capacity for action, not to sow fear.

04:28.460 --> 04:32.940
In this way we reach the sixth section: Conclusion and summary of the first module.

04:33.360 --> 04:38.020
The takeaway from this explanation: Real impact is not measured by the number of followers or shares;

04:38.380 --> 04:40.620
it is measured by the depth of trust we build with people.

04:40.980 --> 04:45.460
We must know our medical boundaries and not cross them, always rely on strong scientific evidence,

04:46.120 --> 04:48.580
and correct any information with respect and understanding.

04:48.980 --> 04:54.700
Combining science with ethics is the magical formula creating health and climate change that endures and makes a difference.

04:54.700 --> 04:59.520
This was our foundational phase, and in this manner we have concluded the first module of our fellowship.

04:59.900 --> 05:02.400
Before bidding you farewell, we leave you with this question for reflection:

05:02.660 --> 05:06.560
If you recall a health or climate rumor that spread in recent times,

05:06.560 --> 05:11.600
how can you apply what we learned to correct it responsibly, respectfully, and without intimidation?

05:11.600 --> 05:16.040
Reflecting on the answer is the first practical step toward becoming a true positive force.

05:16.480 --> 05:20.860
Thank you for your attention, and we will see you in the second module, God willing, with the same enthusiasm.
